<title>UK: Aegon sets $200 million three-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Aegon sets $200 million three-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by</p>
<p>lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett.</p>
<p> BORROWER   Aegon NV</p>
<p> AMT	  $200 MLN  COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    29.AUG.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.031   PAY DATE    29.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    99.856    SPREAD	+15 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LON/AMST  PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  NETHS     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  1.175     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.00 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.AUG.00 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
